Read-only model-path follow-up (Oracle cda51f4d); no new run or source edit.
Probe admission is Control mpsc(8), then exercise -> GuiTask actions(64) -> local outgoing VecDeque -> Wire.out(64) -> one socket writer (stall.rs:507/650; load.rs:589/673/1253-1256). The next stages are server/PTY/ring/logic, then GUI delivery. No per-probe timestamps were captured at these intermediate boundaries.
GUI reader runs on Tokio and forwards through mpsc(8) (load.rs:590). One drain_gui task calls the apply closure synchronously before queuing Applied (load.rs:731-732). That closure applies Grids, rebuilds/publishes and only then queues its ACK. The reader can read independently until its bounded queue fills; that queue's occupancy/time series was not recorded.
The IO apply path calls model::build over all 967 records (load.rs:964; model.rs:872), prepares the 50 watched screens (load.rs:974; model.rs:1185), then publishes (load.rs:976). Production live.rs:264/267/269 and :1124-1132 use the same per-update build/prepare/publish-before-ACK shape. These are IO/Tokio task operations, not UI-thread CPU.
The published-model handoff is Latest ArrayQueue(1), force_push replacing the old entry (bbt-rt/queues.rs:65-82), consumed as an Arc by main.rs:2929. Its occupancy is structurally 0 or 1, not a growing FIFO; publication-to-take delay was not measured. A numeric queue-wait/apply/publish allocation of the 8.359 s is therefore UNPROVEN.
A concrete unmetered path exists: main.rs:3149 calls App::drain before taking the Metal tick. The tick-none early return at :3166-3170 precedes phases.drain assignment at :3172 and every successful-frame meter sample. App::drain can take/project a new Model at :2929/:3004 even when this redraw never encodes. Scene::set_model clones swarms and rebuilds the full seat index/967 SeatRows (scene.rs:421/:460/:468); replacing live_state can drop the old Arc on UI. This path can consume CPU outside the paired successful-frame work; its count/duration was not instrumented, so it is a candidate mechanism, not proof that one particular apply consumed the whole 445 ms gap.
UiEvent::Wake drains the DirtySet at main.rs:3699; wake.rs:51 resets wake admission then, before frame consumption. The retained first-SETTLE witness counts 66459 wake events, message/output/model source wakes 45681/42183/4011. A source can share a wake and these counts are cumulative, not MEASURE-only and not queue depths; do not add them or infer per-function CPU.
A model::build or PanePreparer cost alone cannot directly explain the UI-thread CPU delta: they execute on IO. Conversely the successful-frame phase list omits aborted/tickless redraw work, so the 15.89 ms paired frame phase does not bound all model projection done between completed frames.
Needed before fixing: bounded buffered timestamps/counters for probe enqueue/write, GUI receive/apply-start/apply-end/publish, Latest.take and UI early-return/Scene projection/old-model drop CPU; preserve all workload, publication-before-ACK, timing and idle rules. No new 967 attempt, diagnostic patch or product fix selected in this read-only follow-up.
